[ceiling] The 5 mm clamping flange provides the bare closing land and room for M4 washers and clamps. Its 16 mm margin surrounds the silicone brim on both axes. The 2026-10-05 native Snug slice records bed-rooted interface-5 at print Z50.602–50.880 beneath this band. Cut and detach support at the exposed outer edges before finishing.
file: hardware/printed-parts/zone-c/funnel-mold/cavity.step
click: x=0.000 y=0.000 z=51.150

[ceiling] This underside backs the silicone brim with at least 5 mm shell stock. The 2026-10-05 native Snug slice records bed-rooted interface-4 at print Z44.362–45.600 in the brim band. Cut and detach support through the open dry back before finishing the forming face.
file: hardware/printed-parts/zone-c/funnel-mold/cavity.step
click: x=0.000 y=0.000 z=44.840

[ceiling] This flat underside backs the silicone block with 5 mm shell stock. The 2026-10-05 native Snug slice records bed-rooted interface-2 at print Z1.440–2.640 in the block band. Cut and detach support from the open underside between the three mold feet.
file: hardware/printed-parts/zone-c/funnel-mold/cavity.step
click: x=1.850 y=0.000 z=1.890

[ceiling] This is the dry underside of the lower rod socket. Its 5 mm floor stops the steel rod below the silicone block; it sits 0.7 mm above the feet datum. The 2026-10-05 native Snug slice records bed-rooted interface-1 at print Z0.200–0.480 beneath it. Cut and detach support through the open underside before fitting the rod.
file: hardware/printed-parts/zone-c/funnel-mold/cavity.step
